  "id": "vietnamese_dan_ca_ly",
  "name": "Lý (Central and Southern Vietnamese folk song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Lý is a genre of short strophic folk songs of central and southern Vietnam, sung for leisure and courtship rather than to accompany work, with hundreds of named songs such as lý con sáo, lý ngựa ô and, in Huế, lý mười thương. In the south lý songs belong to the dân ca Nam Bộ repertoire and were absorbed into đờn ca tài tử and cải lương; they are widely recorded by folk singers with đàn tranh, đàn bầu and bamboo flute.",
  "recipe": "classic modern lý, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment, tonal language syllable tone locked melody. dan tranh, dan bau, sao truc. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
